-- **1. Text Length Comparison**

-- > Sometimes a competitor's everyday "used" name is actually longer than their official full name. Identify these specific competitors. Return their official full name and their used name, but only for records where the used name has strictly more characters than the full name.


select
    full_name
    ,used_name
from athletes
    where length(full_name) < length(used_name)
    



;
-- **2. Basic Aggregation & Math**

-- > We are putting together a statistical overview of female competitors. Calculate the overall average height of all female competitors. Return this as a single numerical value, rounded to the nearest whole integer. Be sure to exclude anyone whose height is not recorded.

select
round(avg(height_cm))
from  athletes
where sex = 'Female' and height_cm is not null






;
-- **3. Distinct Values & Filtering**

-- > We need a clean list of the different historical "eras" that countries belong to, but only for countries that have successfully competed in the modern era of the games. Return a deduplicated list of these era names, sorted in alphabetical order.


select distinct 
country_name
,country_era
from nocs
where competed_in_modern_olympics = true
order by country_name asc









;
